# Punctuation this sweep must not touch, because we are quoting somebody else.
#
# One entry per line: <repo-relative path>::<the exact text to leave alone>.
# The scanner blanks each entry out of a file before counting, so a dash inside a
# quotation is invisible to the rule rather than exempt from it.
#
# The bar for adding a line is high, and it got higher on 2026-09-11. The user's rule is
# that the ONLY em dash allowed to survive anywhere in this repo is one inside words
# written by somebody outside this project, in a file belonging to something we use.
# Our own prose, our own comments, our own string literals, our own sample data and our
# own account of the sweep are all out. Where the historical record has to NAME the
# character, it spells it \u2014 rather than typing it, which needs no entry here.
#
# Two places hold one legitimately and neither is listed:
#   docs/original/InvMgr_V1.3.0.html  the preserved original app, 83 of them, never edited
#   tools/m6.6-quotes.allow           this file, which cannot match text without holding it

docs/SPIKE-OD-1.md::"Broken — looking for help"
